WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.108 --> 00:00:19.355
That evening Robin and his men returned to Sherwood Forest with Sir Richard.

2
00:00:19.975 --> 00:00:21.996
Little John had also found some guests.

3
00:00:22.896 --> 00:00:25.137
Robin grinned when he recognized the men.

4
00:00:25.157 --> 00:00:28.979
"Why, it's the Bishop of Hereford and three friars!"

5
00:00:29.259 --> 00:00:29.699
he said.

6
00:00:29.719 --> 00:00:31.800
"Welcome, Bishop!

7
00:00:32.136 --> 00:00:34.657
I haven't seen you since Alan of Dale's wedding."

8
00:00:35.698 --> 00:00:38.399
The bishop paced nervously beneath a tree.

9
00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:41.160
He scowled but didn't say anything.

10
00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.061
He didn't want to join Robin's men for a feast.

11
00:00:44.081 --> 00:00:48.003
"Look at the bishop's horses, Robin," said Little John.

12
00:00:48.563 --> 00:00:49.483
Robin looked over.

13
00:00:50.324 --> 00:00:52.925
Six horses were tied to nearby trees.

14
00:00:53.725 --> 00:00:57.226
Five of them were loaded down with boxes and packs.

15
00:00:58.547 --> 00:01:00.708
Robin's eyes lit up eagerly.

16
00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:03.661
"We'll examine your treasures later, Bishop.

17
00:01:04.322 --> 00:01:06.783
But first I'd like you to meet another guest.

18
00:01:07.403 --> 00:01:09.064
This is Sir Richard."

19
00:01:10.485 --> 00:01:12.066
The bishop scowled again.

20
00:01:12.086 --> 00:01:14.227
"Sir Richard," he snapped.

21
00:01:14.247 --> 00:01:21.071
"I fear that we are companions in this den of His words trailed off as he shot an

22
00:01:21.271 --> 00:01:22.551
uneasy look at Robin.

23
00:01:22.571 --> 00:01:27.674
"Ha-ha!" Robin roared with laughter.

24
00:01:27.694 --> 00:01:29.175
"Go ahead, Bishop.

25
00:01:29.875 --> 00:01:31.016
We won't be insulted.

26
00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:34.442
You were about to say 'den of thieves.'"

27
00:01:35.243 --> 00:01:37.764
Sir Richard laughed, but the bishop did not.

28
00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:42.387
Some of Robin's men went to make fires for roasting meat.

29
00:01:42.407 --> 00:01:47.491
"We should entertain our guests while we wait for dinner," said Robin.

30
00:01:47.511 --> 00:01:50.473
"Let's have an archery contest and some music."

31
00:01:51.494 --> 00:01:54.476
Targets were set up and several men began to shoot.

32
00:01:56.397 --> 00:02:00.340
After the archery contest, a minstrel sang and played the harp.

33
00:02:00.944 --> 00:02:06.308
Meanwhile Robin talked and joked so pleasantly that Sir Richard forgot his troubles.

34
00:02:06.729 --> 00:02:09.011
And the bishop almost forgot his anger.

35
00:02:11.012 --> 00:02:14.135
At last two men came to say that the meal was ready.

36
00:02:14.835 --> 00:02:18.959
There was plenty of good food, and the feast lasted for hours.

37
00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:25.324
When everyone had finished eating, Robin told Sir Richard's sad story to the bishop.

38
00:02:25.344 --> 00:02:28.606
"You're the richest bishop in England," Robin said.

39
00:02:28.626 --> 00:02:30.428
"What can you do to help him?"

40
00:02:31.596 --> 00:02:32.897
The bishop said nothing.

41
00:02:33.658 --> 00:02:36.820
Instead he stared at the ground with a dark expression.

42
00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:38.201
"Little John!"

43
00:02:38.541 --> 00:02:39.222
called Robin.

44
00:02:39.242 --> 00:02:42.264
"It's time to see what the bishop's horses are carrying."

45
00:02:44.366 --> 00:02:46.467
Some men began opening the packs.

46
00:02:47.168 --> 00:02:51.091
The bishop's first horse was carrying silk for a merchant named Quentin.

47
00:02:51.111 --> 00:02:54.493
"I know Quentin," said Robin.

48
00:02:54.513 --> 00:02:58.136
"He's an honest man, so we won't touch his fabric."

49
00:02:58.656 --> 00:03:02.617
The horse's packs also held candles and velvet for a chapel.

50
00:03:02.637 --> 00:03:05.558
"We won't touch the candles either," said Robin.

51
00:03:05.578 --> 00:03:07.298
"They belong in the chapel.

52
00:03:07.879 --> 00:03:10.379
But priests don't need so much velvet.

53
00:03:10.919 --> 00:03:15.901
Divide it into three parts: one to be sold for charity, one for us, and one for the

54
00:03:15.961 --> 00:03:20.682
chapel." Robin examined every item the horses were carrying.

55
00:03:21.342 --> 00:03:23.443
Robin's men repacked some things.

56
00:03:24.023 --> 00:03:26.484
But they divided others into three parts.

57
00:03:27.712 --> 00:03:30.094
The last horse was led before Robin.

58
00:03:30.114 --> 00:03:32.896
"Now what is this one carrying?"

59
00:03:33.197 --> 00:03:33.677
he asked.

60
00:03:33.697 --> 00:03:37.720
"This horse has a box owned by the bishop," said Little John.

61
00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:41.183
"Bishop, do you have the key?"

62
00:03:41.583 --> 00:03:42.364
Robin asked.

63
00:03:43.024 --> 00:03:46.687
The bishop trembled as if he had the chills and shook his head.

64
00:03:46.707 --> 00:03:50.811
"No." "Will Scarlet, break open this box!"

65
00:03:51.151 --> 00:03:51.791
said Robin.

66
00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:59.597
Will struck the box several times with a huge sword and it finally sprang open.

67
00:04:00.257 --> 00:04:04.560
Robin's men gasped as a large heap of gold rolled out.

68
00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:09.342
Robin ordered Will Scarlet and Little John to count it.

69
00:04:10.183 --> 00:04:12.424
Much later Will called out the total.

70
00:04:12.444 --> 00:04:16.146
"Fifteen hundred pounds in gold coins!"

71
00:04:17.066 --> 00:04:18.267
Robin turned to the bishop.

72
00:04:18.287 --> 00:04:20.548
"Where did all this money come from?"

73
00:04:20.968 --> 00:04:21.529
he asked.

74
00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:27.352
"From collecting rents and fines," said a friar.

75
00:04:28.012 --> 00:04:30.213
The bishop glared at him for answering.

76
00:04:30.233 --> 00:04:37.975
"I'll let you keep five hundred pounds, which I hope you'll give to charity," said Robin to the

77
00:04:38.015 --> 00:04:41.816
bishop. "We'll keep five hundred pounds as payment for our feast.

78
00:04:42.356 --> 00:04:43.996
And Sir Richard will get the rest."

79
00:04:44.697 --> 00:04:46.617
Sir Richard looked astonished.

80
00:04:47.257 --> 00:04:48.538
"That's more than I need!"

81
00:04:48.778 --> 00:04:49.198
he said.

82
00:04:49.218 --> 00:04:53.979
"I thank you from the bottom of my heart, and I'll repay you one day."

83
00:04:53.999 --> 00:04:56.820
"That's not necessary," said Robin.

84
00:04:57.888 --> 00:05:00.931
The bishop was grateful that Robin didn't take everything.

85
00:05:01.511 --> 00:05:03.313
Sir Richard mounted his horse.

86
00:05:03.953 --> 00:05:06.936
"I must go for my wife will be anxious about my whereabouts."

87
00:05:09.338 --> 00:05:11.099
The bishop tried to leave too.

88
00:05:11.119 --> 00:05:13.621
"It's getting late.

89
00:05:13.641 --> 00:05:14.722
I must go as well."

90
00:05:14.742 --> 00:05:17.805
"Oh, no," said Robin.

91
00:05:17.825 --> 00:05:21.228
"You're our guest until Sir Richard pays his debt.

92
00:05:21.808 --> 00:05:23.370
I don't want you interfering with that.

93
00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:24.711
But don't worry.

94
00:05:25.151 --> 00:05:26.072
We'll treat you well."

95
00:05:28.284 --> 00:05:31.869
So Robin fed and entertained the bishop for three days.

96
00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:36.475
The bishop had such fun that sometimes he forgot he was a prisoner.

97
00:05:38.317 --> 00:05:44.145
But when he finally left, he said to the friars, "Robin will regret the way he treated us.

98
00:05:44.846 --> 00:05:46.087
I'll make sure of that."
